---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---
<BaseLayout title="Privacy Policy" description="Privacy information for visitors to the TechnoRaise website. This starter policy must be reviewed against actual site operations before launch.">
  <section class="prose-hero section-wrap">
    <span class="section-kicker">YOUR PRIVACY</span><h1>Clear information. <em>Respectful choices.</em></h1>
    <p class="prose-intro">This page is a pre-launch policy template, not a representation that all legal and operational details have been finalized.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-layout section-wrap">
    <aside class="prose-aside"><span>PLEASE NOTE</span><b>Review before<br />public launch.</b></aside>
    <div class="prose-body">
      <h2>Who operates this website</h2><p>The publisher's legal identity, contact details, and applicable jurisdiction have not yet been supplied. They must be added here before public launch.</p>
      <h2>Information collected</h2><p>This publication does not require reader accounts. The hosting provider may process technical request data such as IP addresses and server logs. Optional analytics are loaded only after a visitor chooses “Accept” in the cookie banner; choosing “Reject” keeps that optional analytics script disabled.</p>
      <h2>Cookies and similar technologies</h2><p>The site stores your choice (accepted or rejected) in your browser's local storage so the banner does not reappear on every page. If you accept, Google Tag Manager is loaded and may activate analytics tags configured in that container. If you reject, those optional analytics tags are not loaded. You can change your choice at any time using the Cookie preferences link in the footer. Essential site functionality does not depend on accepting optional analytics.</p>
      <h2>Third-party services</h2><p>The production hosting provider, domain registrar, and any later integrations may process visitor information under their own terms. Identify the actual providers and link to their privacy information before launch.</p>
      <h2>Your rights and choices</h2><p>Applicable privacy rights depend on the publisher's location, visitor location, and the data processing involved. Add the correct rights, request process, and contact channel after obtaining jurisdiction-specific legal review.</p>
      <h2>Policy updates</h2><p>This policy should be dated and updated whenever the site's data practices change. Do not publish this template as a final legal policy without completing that review.</p>
      <p class="policy-warning"><strong>Launch requirement:</strong> Confirm the legal publisher, jurisdiction, hosting provider, logs and retention, cookie behavior, third-party services, and privacy contact before enabling public traffic.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>